.TH "EPX\-SEARCH" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-search \- search documents; read and change search indexes and saved searches
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search [flags]
epx search [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads the Search Service (a preview at Emporix), which searches customers, legal entities and the instances of custom entity types: the documents a search finds, its indexes and saved searches, kept per type, and the jobs that create, update and delete the indexes; changes the indexes and saved searches. A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR. Its writes require the search.search_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx search documents"
Search customers, legal entities or the instances of a custom entity type.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search documents TYPE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the documents of a type that the saved search \fB\-\-saved\-search\fR finds with the text of \fB\-\-text\fR (\fBepx search queries for\-type TYPE\fR lists them): customers, legal entities or the instances of a custom entity type, as a search index holds them. SCORE is how well a document matches; its other fields are only in \fB\-o json\fR. \fB\-\-body\fR gives a search of an index by its own queries and filters instead. An unknown saved search, or index of \fB\-\-body\fR, is not found (exit 4). TYPE is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows; an unknown one has no scope that Emporix grants (exit code 3), and a type created in the last minutes has none yet. Known limitation: for customer or legal\-entity, epx requests the read scope that finds every document, so a credential that holds only a restricted one, such as customer.customer_read\-\-DE, or only the own\-read scope, such as customer.customer_read_own, fails with exit code 3.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole. In place of custom.<type>_read, customer requires customer.customer_read; legal\-entity requires customermanagement.legalentity_read.
.PP
Requires the search.search_read, custom.<type>_read scopes. <type> is the custom entity type in lower case (custom.document_read for DOCUMENT).
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, SCORE.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-saved\-search <ID>\fR
The ID of the saved search to run (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-text <text>\fR
The text to search for in every term of the saved search (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.SS "epx search indexes"
Read, upsert, delete, export and import search indexes.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes [flags]
epx search indexes [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads search indexes: which fields of the documents of a type can be searched. STATUS is building, ready or failed and FIELDS the indexed fields (\fB\-o json\fR shows how each is searched). \fB\-\-query\fR matches STATUS in upper case (\fBstatus:READY\fR; \fBstatus:ready\fR matches no index). Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. A search index kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is listed too; \fBepx api\fR reaches it by its path, such as \fBepx api get /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/indexes/ID \-\-scope search.search_read\fR.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR. Its writes require the search.search_manage scope.
.SS "epx search indexes delete"
Delete a search index.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes delete TYPE ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Starts the job that deletes the search index ID of the type TYPE: Emporix answers with the job\(aqs id (\fBepx search jobs get ID\fR reads the job), and with 409 Conflict (exit 5) while another job of the index is running. A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. TYPE and ID are a search index\(aqs type and ID, as \fBepx search indexes list\fR shows them. A search index kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is deleted with \fBepx api delete /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/indexes/ID \-\-scope search.search_manage\fR.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-wait\fR then reads the job again every \fB\-\-poll\-interval\fR, as \fBepx search jobs get\fR does and with the search.search_read scope too, saying on standard error how its status changes, until it ends: then it prints the job and exits 0 if it ended success, else 1. When \fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR passes first, it prints the job as last read and exits 1; the job goes on. When a read of the job fails, it prints the job as last read and exits as that read does, e.g. 4 when the job is not found.
.PP
As Emporix answers with the id of the job alone, \fB\-\-wait\fR reads the job by that id first. Where Emporix answers with none, having started no job, \fB\-\-wait\fR prints the response and says so (exit 0); where no read of the job succeeds, it prints the response.
.PP
Requires the search.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-poll\-interval <duration>\fR
How often \fB\-\-wait\fR reads the index job, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB5s\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the index job ends, then print it.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout <duration>\fR
How long \fB\-\-wait\fR waits, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB30m\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx search indexes export"
Export search indexes.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes export [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads an export package of the search indexes that \fB\-\-index\fR names, as TYPE/ID (the TYPE and ID that \fBepx search indexes list\fR shows): their configuration, without status or metadata. Emporix answers an unknown index as not found (exit 4). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. A search index kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is exported with \fB\-\-body\fR. Emporix refuses an empty selection (\fB\-\-body\fR with [], exit 1).
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole. DATA is the package, base64\-encoded and cut in the table; \fB\-o json\fR prints the package whole, as an import on another tenant takes it.
.PP
Requires the search.search_manage scope. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR
Opt in to requesting search.search_manage, which can also change data (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among DATA, EXPORTED AT.
.TP
\fB\-\-index <TYPE/ID>\fR
A search index to export, as TYPE/ID (repeatable; required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx search indexes for\-type"
List the search indexes of a type.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes for\-type TYPE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads search indexes: which fields of the documents of a type can be searched. STATUS is building, ready or failed and FIELDS the indexed fields (\fB\-o json\fR shows how each is searched). \fB\-\-query\fR matches STATUS in upper case (\fBstatus:READY\fR; \fBstatus:ready\fR matches no index). Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. A search index kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is listed too; \fBepx api\fR reaches it by its path, such as \fBepx api get /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/indexes/ID \-\-scope search.search_read\fR. TYPE is the type of search indexes, as \fBepx search indexes list\fR shows it; an unknown type lists nothing.
.PP
Requires the search.search_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, NAME, STATUS, FIELDS, VERSION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx search indexes get"
Show one search index.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes get TYPE ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads search indexes: which fields of the documents of a type can be searched. STATUS is building, ready or failed and FIELDS the indexed fields (\fB\-o json\fR shows how each is searched). \fB\-\-query\fR matches STATUS in upper case (\fBstatus:READY\fR; \fBstatus:ready\fR matches no index). Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. A search index kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is listed too; \fBepx api\fR reaches it by its path, such as \fBepx api get /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/indexes/ID \-\-scope search.search_read\fR. TYPE and ID are a search index\(aqs type and ID, as \fBepx search indexes list\fR shows them; an unknown one is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Requires the search.search_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, NAME, STATUS, FIELDS, VERSION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx search indexes import"
Import search indexes.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes import [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates or updates each search index of the export package in \fB\-\-file\fR, as update does. The package is the whole response of \fBepx search indexes export \-o json\fR, with its exportedAt (Emporix answers 400 without it). Emporix answers with a result per index, in the order of the package, with the id of the job that builds it where one started. When an index fails, those before it stay created or updated, and Emporix answers with the error of the one that failed (409 Conflict, exit 5, while a job of it is running or when its metadata.version is stale).
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-wait\fR then reads the job again every \fB\-\-poll\-interval\fR, as \fBepx search jobs get\fR does and with the search.search_read scope too, saying on standard error how its status changes, until it ends: then it prints the job and exits 0 if it ended success, else 1. When \fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR passes first, it prints the job as last read and exits 1; the job goes on. When a read of the job fails, it prints the job as last read and exits as that read does, e.g. 4 when the job is not found.
.PP
As Emporix answers with the id of each job alone, in a result per item that names its type/id, \fB\-\-wait\fR reads each job by its id first and follows the jobs in turn, all within \fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR, naming each by that type/id. It prints the jobs as last read in place of the results, as a JSON array in their order, leaving out each job never read (standard error says why), and exits 0 only if each ended success; where jobs failed with different exit codes, 1. Where Emporix started no job, it prints [] and says so (exit 0).
.PP
Requires the search.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-poll\-interval <duration>\fR
How often \fB\-\-wait\fR reads the index job, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB5s\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the index job ends, then print it.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout <duration>\fR
How long \fB\-\-wait\fR waits, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB30m\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes import \-\-file indexes.json \-\-dry\-run
epx search indexes import \-\-file indexes.json \-\-wait \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
