.SS "epx search indexes update"
Upsert a search index.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes update TYPE ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the search index ID of the type TYPE, or replaces it (an upsert), with the one in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object with its fields (each with its path and how it is searched) and optionally name and description. A job builds a new index, and one whose fields changed or that is building or failed: Emporix then answers 202 Accepted with the job\(aqs id (\fBepx search jobs get ID\fR reads the job), else 204 No Content. With metadata.version, as \fBepx search indexes get TYPE ID \-o json\fR prints it, Emporix replaces only that version; another, or a job of the index that is still running, is a conflict (exit 5). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. TYPE and ID are a search index\(aqs type and ID, as \fBepx search indexes list\fR shows them, or a new ID. A search index kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is upserted with \fBepx api put /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/indexes/ID \-\-scope search.search_manage \-\-file FILE\fR.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-wait\fR then reads the job again every \fB\-\-poll\-interval\fR, as \fBepx search jobs get\fR does and with the search.search_read scope too, saying on standard error how its status changes, until it ends: then it prints the job and exits 0 if it ended success, else 1. When \fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR passes first, it prints the job as last read and exits 1; the job goes on. When a read of the job fails, it prints the job as last read and exits as that read does, e.g. 4 when the job is not found.
.PP
As Emporix answers with the id of the job alone, \fB\-\-wait\fR reads the job by that id first. Where Emporix answers with none, having started no job, \fB\-\-wait\fR prints the response and says so (exit 0); where no read of the job succeeds, it prints the response.
.PP
Requires the search.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-poll\-interval <duration>\fR
How often \fB\-\-wait\fR reads the index job, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB5s\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the index job ends, then print it.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout <duration>\fR
How long \fB\-\-wait\fR waits, 1s or more (only with \fB\-\-wait\fR). Default: \fB30m\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search indexes update VEHICLE vehicles \-\-file index.json \-\-dry\-run
epx search indexes update VEHICLE vehicles \-\-file index.json \-\-wait \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx search jobs"
Read index jobs.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search jobs [flags]
epx search jobs [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the jobs that create, update and delete search indexes: TYPE is create_index, update_index or delete_index, STATUS in_progress, success or failure as the table and JSON show them, and RESULT what the job recorded when it finished. \fB\-\-query\fR matches the upper\-case form (\fBstatus:SUCCESS\fR and \fBtype:UPDATE_INDEX\fR are checked; a lower\-case filter, such as \fBstatus:success\fR, matches no job). Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1).
.PP
Requires the search.search_read scope.
.SS "epx search jobs get"
Show one index job.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search jobs get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the jobs that create, update and delete search indexes: TYPE is create_index, update_index or delete_index, STATUS in_progress, success or failure as the table and JSON show them, and RESULT what the job recorded when it finished. \fB\-\-query\fR matches the upper\-case form (\fBstatus:SUCCESS\fR and \fBtype:UPDATE_INDEX\fR are checked; a lower\-case filter, such as \fBstatus:success\fR, matches no job). Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1).
.PP
Requires the search.search_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, STATUS, INDEX, CREATED, MODIFIED, RESULT.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx search jobs list"
List index jobs.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search jobs list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the jobs that create, update and delete search indexes: TYPE is create_index, update_index or delete_index, STATUS in_progress, success or failure as the table and JSON show them, and RESULT what the job recorded when it finished. \fB\-\-query\fR matches the upper\-case form (\fBstatus:SUCCESS\fR and \fBtype:UPDATE_INDEX\fR are checked; a lower\-case filter, such as \fBstatus:success\fR, matches no job). Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1).
.PP
Requires the search.search_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, STATUS, INDEX, CREATED, MODIFIED, RESULT.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx search queries"
Read, upsert and delete saved searches.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search queries [flags]
epx search queries [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads saved searches: queries and filters (only in \fB\-o json\fR) stored to run against a search INDEX of a type. Emporix answers a list\(aqs malformed \fB\-\-query\fR with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. A saved search kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is listed too; \fBepx api\fR reaches it by its path, such as \fBepx api get /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/queries/ID \-\-scope search.search_read\fR.
.PP
Its reads require the search.search_read scope. Its writes require the search.search_manage scope.
.SS "epx search queries delete"
Delete a saved search.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search queries delete TYPE ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the saved search ID of the type TYPE; an unknown one is not found (exit 4). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. TYPE and ID are a saved search\(aqs type and ID, as \fBepx search queries list\fR shows them. A saved search kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is deleted with \fBepx api delete /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/queries/ID \-\-scope search.search_manage\fR.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the search.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx search queries for\-type"
