.SS "epx search queries update"
Upsert a saved search.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search queries update TYPE ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the saved search ID of the type TYPE, or replaces it (an upsert), with the one in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object with index (the ID of a search index of TYPE), queries, filters or both, and optionally name and description. Emporix answers a new one with its id (201 Created), and a replaced one with 204 No Content. Replacing one needs its metadata.version, as \fBepx search queries get TYPE ID \-o json\fR prints it; a stale one is a conflict (exit 5). An unknown index is not found (exit 4). A type is customer or legal\-entity, exactly as written, or a custom entity type, whose ID \fBepx custom\-entities list\fR shows. TYPE and ID are a saved search\(aqs type and ID, as \fBepx search queries list\fR shows them, or a new ID. A saved search kept under another spelling of a built\-in type, such as CUSTOMER, is upserted with \fBepx api put /search/{tenant}/search/CUSTOMER/queries/ID \-\-scope search.search_manage \-\-file FILE\fR.
.PP
Localized text in the body is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Acme", "de": "Acme"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent with Content\-Language: *. Emporix refuses a string in its place.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the search.search_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx search queries update VEHICLE by\-make \-\-file by\-make.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
